UnitMetarouter::constructor
├── when the wrapped native token is the zero address
│   └── it should deploy with a zero WETH
├── when the voter is the zero address
│   ├── it should deploy without reading the voter
│   ├── it should set IS_ROOT to false
│   └── it should leave EMISSION_TOKEN, STAKING_ESCROW, STAKING_TOKEN and RELAY_FACTORY as zero
├── when the position manager is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the interchain account router is the zero address
│   └── it should deploy with ICA_ROUTER as zero
├── when the factory registry is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the native mirror token is the zero address
│   └── it should leave the native mirror scale as zero
├── when the wrapped native token is the native mirror token
│   └── it should revert with WethIsNativeErc20
├── when the native mirror token reports more decimals than native
│   └── it should revert with InvalidNativeErc20Decimals
├── when the native mirror token reports the native decimals
│   └── it should set the native mirror scale to one
├── when the native mirror token reports fewer decimals than native
│   └── it should derive the native mirror scale from the decimals difference
├── when the native mirror token reports the stablecoin six decimals
│   └── it should set the native mirror scale to the known trillion factor
├── when the local chain is not the root chain
│   ├── it should derive the emission token from the leaf voter receipt token
│   └── it should set IS_ROOT to false and STAKING_ESCROW, STAKING_TOKEN and RELAY_FACTORY to zero
├── when the local chain id is below the root chain id
│   └── it should set IS_ROOT to false
└── given the local chain is the root chain
    ├── when the root voter is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── given the root voter is a valid address
        ├── when the relay factory is the zero address
        │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
        └── when the relay factory is a valid address
            ├── it should derive the emission token from the root voter minter
            ├── it should set IS_ROOT to true
            ├── it should derive STAKING_ESCROW from the root voter and STAKING_TOKEN from the escrow TOKEN
            └── it should set RELAY_FACTORY to the relay factory

UnitMetarouter::executeSubPlan
├── given the sub plan fails
│   ├── when the sub plan is unflagged
│   │   └── it should revert the batch
│   ├── when the sub plan is flagged
│   │   └── it should unwind the nested changes and continue
│   └── when the sub plan is flagged after the outer plan funds the token
│       └── it should sweep the complete funded balance to the fallback recipient
└── when the sub plan succeeds
    └── it should apply the nested command state changes

UnitMetarouter::msgSender
├── when a batch is active
│   └── it should return the outer caller
└── when a batch is not active
    └── it should return the zero address

UnitMetarouter::balanceCheck
├── given the asset is a token
│   ├── given the balance is below the minimum
│   │   ├── when the command is unflagged
│   │   │   └── it should revert the whole batch with InsufficientBalance for _token
│   │   └── when the command is flagged
│   │       ├── it should revert only the inner call
│   │       └── it should continue the batch
│   ├── when the balance meets the minimum
│   │   └── it should pass
│   └── when the checked token is the native mirror token held by the execution address
│       └── it should revert even if the total balance meets the minimum through pre batch funds
└── given the asset is native
    ├── when the owner is the execution address and the available balance is below the minimum
    │   └── it should revert even if the total balance meets the minimum through pre batch funds
    ├── when the owner is the execution address and the available balance meets the minimum
    │   └── it should pass
    ├── when the owner is another account and the live native balance is below the minimum
    │   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance
    └── when the owner is another account and the live native balance meets the minimum
        └── it should check the account's live native balance

UnitMetarouter::receive
├── when the sender is unexpected and no batch is active
│   └── it should revert with InvalidEthSender
├── when the sender is the wrapped native token
│   └── it should accept the native eth
└── when a batch is active
    └── it should accept the native eth

UnitMetarouter::onErc721Received
├── when no batch is active
│   └── it should revert with BatchNotActive
└── given a batch is active
    ├── when the sender is not the position manager
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidNftSender
    ├── when no expected nft is set
    │   └── it should revert with UnexpectedNftSender
    └── given an expected nft is set
        ├── when the from is not the expected sender
        │   └── it should revert with UnexpectedNftSender
        ├── when the token id is not the expected one
        │   └── it should revert with UnexpectedNftSender
        └── when the from and token id are the expected ones
            ├── it should track the collection and token id
            ├── it should leave the expected nft for the setting command to clear
            └── it should return the selector
